  {
   "key": "scene_07",
   "text": "Here is what the scoreline hides. Data from FotMob gives expected goals of 1.39 for Germany and 1.11 for the Netherlands. Almost level. The Dutch number rests on one header: Malen's, in minute 25. That single chance is 0.69 of the 1.11. Germany's five goals came from smaller chances: 0.03, 0.05, 0.13, 0.24 and 0.26. Germany took the chances the Dutch spurned. They also shot more: 18 shots to 9, and 10 on target to 1. So it was not just luck. Germany shot more, and shot straighter.",
