  {
   "key": "scene_09",
   "text": "At his unveiling, Klopp said: \"I want people to go home thinking 'Wow, that was cool!'\" That was FIFA.com quoting him. A first home defeat to Greece has become a quarter-final place. So, the answer. This was a game close on chances that Germany won in the box, and the Dutch lost there. Germany had 50 touches in the opposition box, the Netherlands 19. And for Xavi, it all comes back to one header, Malen's 0.69 miss at minute 25. Tell me in the comments: was Malen's miss the moment the night tipped? And if you like football told through the numbers, subscribe to The Other Touchline.",
